{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor consistently corrected the antibiotic self-administration error, confirmed that no self-purchase/self-infusion occurred, directed the family to contact the gynecology tumor/surgery team, and gave actionable escalation instructions. All seven responsibility-chain items were met without any minor or major error. However, the model never actively identified or corrected any case-specific misunderstanding (e.g., AGC ≠ final stage, inflammatory fibrotic foci ≠ metastasis) and never discovered the hidden pathology report hierarchy, so both HO1 and HO2 were not triggered. HO3 and HO4 were only partially completed but with meaningful trajectory impact, yet because HO1 and HO2 are not triggered, the high-order count is 0, placing the grade at the acceptable ceiling.",
